[{:db/id 17592186347044 :question/problem "$$\n{∭}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}V={\\int }_{∗}^{∗}{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{∗}^{∗}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx\n$$\n\nThe triple integral above is defined over the type III region given by\n\n$$\nS={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le z\\le 2x,\\,0\\le y\\le xz}.\n$$\n\nFor a fixed admissible $x$, let $[a(x),b(x)]$ be the full nonempty $z$ fiber of the exactly specified region $S$. What is $a(x)+b(x)$?" :question/worked-solution "The defining set $S$ is retained exactly. The requirement $0\\le z\\le2x$ has no solution for $x<0$, so the actual outer range is $0\\le x\\le2$. For each such $x$, the full $z$ interval is $[0,2x]$, and $xz\\ge0$ makes the $y$ interval $[0,xz]$ nonempty. Hence\n\n$$a(x)+b(x)=0+2x=2x,\\qquad \\iiint_S f\\,dV=\\int_0^2\\int_0^{2x}\\int_0^{xz}f(x,y,z)\\,dy\\,dz\\,dx.$$\n\nFor $f=1$, the true volume is $\\int_0^2 2x^3\\,dx=8$. The source solution retained the nominal outer range $[-1,2]$ and included reversed $z$ bounds on negative $x$, giving the signed value $15/2$. That outer-bound error does not change the requested middle-endpoint sum $2x$." :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
